.TH SET_ADDSA 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
set_addsa \- Add an element from a stralloc to a set

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/set.h>
.IB #include <lib/stralloc.h>

.IB int
.IB set_addsa(set_t* set, const stralloc* sa);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBset_addsa\fR function adds an element from a stralloc to a set. It takes a set and a stralloc, and adds the element from the stralloc to the set.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB set
The set to add the element to.
.TP
.IB sa
The stralloc containing the element to add.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns 0 if the element was successfully added to the set, or -1 if an error occurred.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBset_addsa\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/set.h>
#include <lib/stralloc.h>

int main() {
    set_t set;
    stralloc sa;
    stralloc_init(&sa);
    stralloc_copy(&sa, "apple");

    set_init(&set);
    if (set_addsa(&set, &sa) == 0) {
        printf("Element added to set.\n");
    } else {
        printf("Failed to add element to set.\n");
    }

    set_free(&set);
    stralloc_free(&sa);
    return 0;
}
.nef